{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-214472",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have $5\\in [a]_{9}$ if \n\n$$\n5≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $5\\in [14]_{9}$ because $5≡14\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\in [-4]_{9}$ because $5≡-4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\notin [17]_{9}$ because $5≢17\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
